From ce21a5cf3d1fd92b84ea9ad2b7c7240aff2162d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hrvoje Nuic <hrvoje.nuic@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 23:26:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Bluetooth: btusb: Add Mercusys MA530 for Realtek RTL8761BUV

Add the USB ID for the Mercusys MA530 Bluetooth adapter. The device uses
a Realtek RTL8761BUV controller and works with the existing Realtek setup
path.

The device reports vendor ID 0x2c4e and product ID 0x0115, and loads the
rtl_bt/rtl8761bu_fw.bin firmware successfully with this quirk.

Provenance
----------
Origin:       ce21a5cf3d1fd92b84ea9ad2b7c7240aff2162d2
              "Bluetooth: btusb: Add Mercusys MA530 for Realtek RTL8761BUV"
              torvalds/linux, authored 2026-04-22, committed 2026-06-11 by
              Luiz Augusto von Dentz via bluetooth-next -> net-next
              (merge 9bbdc7dc4090, "for-net-next-2026-06-11").
Author:       Hrvoje Nuic <hrvoje.nuic@gmail.com>
Upstream:     YES -- and this is the first patch in this series for which that
              is true. Every other carried patch is fork-only code mainline
              does not have; this one is a plain BACKPORT of a mainline commit
              that has simply not reached the stable line we pin. Verified by
              tag, not inferred: absent from v7.0 and v7.1, present in
              v7.2-rc1 and v7.2 final, so v7.2 is its first release. It is
              also absent from every 6.18.y up to and including the pinned
              6.18.45 (the commit carries no Cc: stable, so it is not queued
              for that line and no bump inside 6.18.y will bring it in).
              DELETE THIS PATCH the moment the kernel pin leaves 6.18.y for
              7.2 or newer -- at that point the ID is in-tree and re-adding it
              would collide.
Backport:     v7.2 -> 6.18.45, Michael C. Ferguson, 2026-08-24. Zero edits --
              the hunk is byte-identical to the mainline commit's, because the
              context it anchors on has not moved across the whole 6.18.y line.
              Verified to apply at -F0 (Buildroot's fuzz setting, so an offset
              is allowed and fuzz is not) against pristine btusb.c from
              v6.18.45 (0 offset), v6.18.44 (0), and v6.18.38 (-2) -- the last
              being the base scripts/export-kernel-tree.sh replays onto.
Fork:         MiSTer-devel/Linux-Kernel_MiSTer landed the same two lines
              independently as 6332499e7 ("Bluetooth: btusb: add Mercusys
              2c4e:0115 support (#78)", 2026-08-24, Stanislav Ponomarev),
              which is what scripts/check-fork-sync.sh flagged. That commit and
              this patch are the same change; the record for it is
              docs/kernel-recon/records/6332499e7545499dc361d09af7b44b33f494fe5d.json.
              This file names the MAINLINE commit as its origin because that is
              where the code came from and who wrote it.
Not in beta:  deliberately absent from board/mister/de10nano/linux-patches-beta/
              series -- the RT variant pins 7.2, which already carries the ID
              in-tree. Not merely redundant there: MEASURED, the same -F0
              dry-run against v7.2's btusb.c is "Hunk #1 FAILED at 786", so
              listing it would break `make rt` at patch time rather than
              apply twice. This is the beta series' ONLY exclusion, and that
              file's header records it.
Hardware:     Mercusys MA550H (tested by the fork's contributor) and MA530
              (tested by the mainline author). Not tested here -- we have
              neither adapter. The risk of being wrong is a dongle that
              still does not bind, never a regression: the entry is one row
              in a device-ID table that nothing else reads.
Firmware:     already shipped. rtl_bt/rtl8761bu_fw.bin and
              rtl8761bu_config.bin come from BR2_PACKAGE_LINUX_FIRMWARE_RTL_87XX_BT
              (docs/firmware-parity.md), and CONFIG_BT_RTL / CONFIG_BT_HCIBTUSB_RTL
              are already on, so the ID entry was the only missing piece.
---
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
index ea9df7d..46931fc 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -786,6 +786,8 @@ static const struct usb_device_id quirks_table[] = {
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x2ff8, 0xb011), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK },
 
 	/* Additional Realtek 8761BUV Bluetooth devices */
+	{ USB_DEVICE(0x2c4e, 0x0115), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
+						     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH },
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x2357, 0x0604), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
 						     BTUSB_WIDEBAND_SPEECH },
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x0b05, 0x190e), .driver_info = BTUSB_REALTEK |
